##
## display.json holds how the charts look, as set under [DisplayOptions]. The JSON
## generator writes the readings and meta.json, and none of it says how to show them.
## weewx-json.js fetches display.json beside them. The file has one copy per report,
## so a report in another language has the labels in that language. For example:
##
##   {"periods": ["day", "week"], "time_lengths": {"day": 97200, "week": 604800},
##    "plot_groups": ["tempdew", "rain"], "telemetry_plot_groups": ["rx"],
##    "charts": {"rain": {"plot_type": "bar", "yscale": [null, null, null],
##                        "vector_rotate": 90,
##                        "series": {"rain": {"label": "Rain (hourly total)"}}}},
##    "labels": {"outTemp": "Outside Temperature", ...},
##    "units": {"report": {"group_temperature": "degree_C", ...},
##              "labels": {"degree_C": "°C", ...}, "formats": {"degree_C": "%.1f", ...}}}
##
## 'charts' holds the options of each plot group, with the defaults under [[Charts]]
## filled in. A series is listed only where [[Charts]] gives it an option of its own.
## 'labels' holds the generic label of each observation type. A series without a label
## of its own takes the one of its type.
##
## This file holds what concerns the charts and the units. What concerns the page
## itself, e.g., the texts of its buttons, the station and the forecast, goes inline
## into the page by scripts.inc.
